## Dead Ends
Cancelling only the new cache tasks cannot release a pre-existing scheduler actor reference cycle. No scheduler queue, scoring, accounting, or cleanup algorithm change was needed; weakening only the installed observer ownership resolves the cycle while preserving live callbacks.

## Hints for Future Agents
The scheduler actor owns slots and their installed observer. A strong lease-manager observer leads through SchedulerBookingCleanup back to a strong admission command sender. Keep this observer weak. Deferred admission callbacks must still replay when the observer is installed, and callbacks after manager destruction must be harmless.

